messages:
Anya P: Quick sync — PR #4520 updates a bunch of SDK snippets (py/ts/go). We rolled the new streaming iterator + renamed pagination tokens last week. Need minimal migration snippets and one short migration blurb.
Sam W: Ill take Go. Plan: show old Chunks() -> new StreamIter() example and a tiny pagination mapping line.
Lina H: Ill do Python streaming + a 2-line retry helper demonstrating exponential backoff. Will add the 'dont retry on 4xx' line.
Omar Z: Taking TypeScript examples and will scan for broken anchors. Also will ensure the TS snippet uses async iteration idiom.
docs-bot: CI: linkcheck flagged /docs/streams-legacy.md -> 404 for PR #4520.
Anya P: Replace the broken link with /docs/streams and add the migration note: "page -> page_token, per_page -> page_size; responses include next_page_token." Keep migration paragraph one short sentence.
Sam W: Go snippet (old vs new):
```go
// old
resp, _ := client.Stream(ctx, req)
for c := range resp.Chunks() {
  fmt.Println(c.Text)
}

// new
it := client.StreamIter(ctx, req)
for it.Next() {
  fmt.Println(it.Value().Text)
}
```
Lina H: Python snippet + tiny retry:
```py
from time import sleep

def tiny_retry(fn, tries=3):
  for i in range(tries):
    try: return fn()
    except TransientError:
      sleep(min(2**i, 5))
  raise

with client.stream_iter(prompt) as it:
  for chunk in it:
    print(chunk.text)
# note: do not retry on 4xx client errors
```
Omar Z: TypeScript snippet (async iterator):
```ts
// old event-style
const s = client.stream(req)
s.on('data', c => console.log(c.text))

// new async iterator
for await (const chunk of client.streamIter(req)) {
  console.log(chunk.text)
}
```
Sam W: Also added one-line pagination mapping in the migration note: `page -> page_token, per_page -> page_size` and example of reading `next_page_token` from responses.
Lina H: I trimmed the retry so its clearly a snippet, added the one-liner about 4xx, and included a short sentence that pagination tokens are explicit now.
Omar Z: Ran local build after swapping the link; preview deploy link created: https://deploy-preview-4520--docs.redwood.ai (linkcheck passed).
Anya P: Looks good. If CI stays green Ill merge in ~30m. Thanks all for keeping snippets small and copy-paste friendly.
